/target
/target-container
# Feature- and profile-varying builds get their own target dir, so an
# instrumented binary never overwrites the release one under the same
# path. Building dhat into the default dir once cost a performance
# review its whole measurement set: every later "release" run silently
# re-executed the instrumented binary at ~5x slower, with nothing in
# the output saying so.
/target-dhat
/target-prof
# The host-native validation run (`cargo` outside the container), kept apart
# from `/target` so a host check never invalidates the container's cache.
/target-host
/tmp/
/dhat-heap.json
/flamegraph.svg
/perf.data
/perf.data.old
__pycache__/
python_draft/__pycache__/
.tally-config.toml
gatk/
freebayes/
samtools/
htslib/
sdust/
bcftools/
gatk-protected/
TRTools/
HipSTR/
GangSTR/
TRF-mod/
# `/CLAUDE.md` was ignored until 2026-08-04. It is tracked now, deliberately:
# it is the only file loaded into an assistant's context automatically, and
# while it was ignored it existed **only in the main checkout**. Every git
# worktree silently lost it — including the project's own writing rules, which
# were then broken for two days in a worktree that had never seen them.
# `ai/skills/` is tracked and reaches every worktree; the file that says to use
# the skills has to travel the same way.
/.claude/
benchmarks/tomato1/crams/
benchmarks/tomato1/results/**
# ...but keep the small perf result TSVs (reference snapshots the dashboard reads).
!benchmarks/tomato1/results/perf/
!benchmarks/tomato1/results/perf/*.tsv
benchmarks/human_genome_bottle/crams/
benchmarks/human_genome_bottle/results/
benchmarks/human_genome_bottle/results_nobaq/
# SSR benchmark: derived results are local. Glob covers results/,
# results_smoke6/, results_cmp6/, results_full63/, and any future results*
# dir (VCFs + .ssr.psp are large, never committed).
benchmarks/ssr_tomato1/results*
# SSR-targeted crams (sliced on rick from the whole-genome crams against
# ssr_regions.bed). Large; never committed. The ssr_regions.bed that defines
# them IS tracked (small, reproducible from the catalog + seed).
benchmarks/ssr_tomato1/crams/
# marimo per-notebook session cache (machine-specific, auto-generated)
__marimo__/
# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

# Claude Code personal overrides (not for commit)
.claude/settings.local.json

# GIAB human benchmark: track the runner/analysis scripts and README, but keep
# the heavy local data out of git (reference genome, BAM/CRAM, truth VCFs,
# generated .psp/.vcf results — gigabytes, fetched/built locally).
benchmarks/giab/*
!benchmarks/giab/src/
!benchmarks/giab/README.md

# GIAB HG002 STR coverage benchmark: track the runner/analysis scripts + README,
# keep the heavy local data out (BAMs, catalog .cat, truth/regions, .psp/.vcf
# results, HipSTR logs, eval_table.tsv — gigabytes, built locally from the scripts).
benchmarks/ssr_hg002/*
!benchmarks/ssr_hg002/src/
!benchmarks/ssr_hg002/scripts/
!benchmarks/ssr_hg002/README.txt
benchmarks/ssr_hg002/scripts/__marimo__/

# tomato2 hidden-paralog-filter study: track the scripts + the region definition,
# keep the heavy/derivable data out (CRAMs, .psp, windowed coverage, VCF/parquet
# results — gigabytes, all built locally from the scripts).
benchmarks/tomato2/*
!benchmarks/tomato2/src/
!benchmarks/tomato2/regions_n160_200kb.bed
!benchmarks/tomato2/README.md
# SSR tomato benchmark: the ng repeat catalog is derived from the reference and
# is large. It cannot live beside the reference the way GRCh38's does, because
# `$HOME/genomes` is mounted read-only, so it is built here instead.
benchmarks/ssr_tomato1/catalog/
